---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites<br/>EditSiteModal
    participant SitePage as Site page<br/>/detail/[namesite]
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.3 and 2.0.5. Part 1 (2.0.3) exists: handleSaveSite calls updateSite and toggleSiteActive,<br/>and both check the caller on the server with requireApprovedAdmin().<br/>Part 2 (2.0.5, edit mode on the Site page) is Proposed.<br/><br/>Part 1: US 2.0.3 Deactivate or reactivate a Site
    Admin->>Page: Open EditSiteModal, set Active on or off, select Save (AT1)
    activate Page
    Page->>Actions: updateSite(id, namesite, ab_county), then<br/>toggleSiteActive(id, is_active) only if is_active changed (exist)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin() (exists)
    alt Caller is not an Admin
        Actions-->>Page: Throw 'Only admins can edit sites.', no change
        Page-->>Admin: alert() with the error
    else Caller is an Admin
        Actions->>DB: Update sites_pa namesite, ab_county,<br/>then is_active only if it changed
        activate DB
        alt Update fails
            DB-->>Actions: Error
            Actions-->>Page: Throw error
            Page-->>Admin: alert() with the error (existing)
        else Update done
            DB-->>Actions: OK
            Actions-->>Page: OK
            Page-->>Admin: Show the new status in the list
        end
        deactivate DB
    end
    deactivate Actions
    deactivate Page
    Note over Admin,DB: getSitesOnline and getSiteByName read only is_active Sites. An inactive Site leaves pickers<br/>and search (AT2) and comes back after reactivation (AT3). Gap for AT4: getSiteByName also hides<br/>the Site page of an inactive Site, so its SIRs cannot be viewed. This needs a change (Proposed).<br/><br/>Part 2: US 2.0.5 Update the fields of a Site page (Proposed)
    Admin->>SitePage: Select "Edit mode"
    activate SitePage
    SitePage->>Actions: getSitePageFields(siteId) (Proposed)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server
    alt Caller is not an Admin (AT2)
        Actions-->>SitePage: Refuse (403)
        SitePage-->>Admin: Stay in view mode, show "Admins only"
    else Caller is an Admin
        Actions->>DB: Read site_page_fields rows and their<br/>is_visible flags (proposed)
        activate DB
        DB-->>Actions: Fields
        deactivate DB
        Actions-->>SitePage: Fields
        SitePage-->>Admin: Show each field with a clear shown or hidden mark (AT1, AT3)
        Admin->>SitePage: Change values, identify the steward who supplied them,<br/>optionally select the source SIR, set shown or hidden, and select Save
        SitePage->>Actions: updateSitePageFields(siteId, fields,<br/>providedByStewardId, sourceResponseId) (Proposed)
        Actions->>Actions: Check Admin role again
        Actions->>DB: Update site_page_fields with provided_by_steward_id<br/>and optional source_response_id
        activate DB
        alt Update fails
            DB-->>Actions: Error
            Actions-->>SitePage: Error
            SitePage-->>Admin: Show the error and stay in edit mode
        else Update done
            DB-->>Actions: OK
            Actions-->>SitePage: OK
            SitePage-->>Admin: Show new fields and remove hidden fields (AT4)
        end
        deactivate DB
    end
    deactivate Actions
    deactivate SitePage

    Note over Admin,DB: Decision for US 2.0.5: each saved field records the steward who supplied it.<br/>When the value came from a SIR, it also records that source response.
